{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779211854,"nonce":"dG70+e9Ggtyt1FmWCau7qFbz0Mo=","message":"## Follow-up: task timeline/value editor needed for eval and task overrides\n\nCreated `bd5aefb` for the generalized authoring surface behind the delayed-task and eval-override questions raised during browser review.\n\nPipeline relevance here:\n\n- Training stages should not expose delayed-task internals as raw arrays. The task editor should render epochs, signal lanes, length ranges/distributions, target/go/hold semantics, catch-trial probability, and endpoint generation as editable controls with preview.\n- Eval stages need the same value system for overrides: SISU, perturbation/intervention profiles, task variants, target generation, temporal metric windows, and robustness sweeps.\n- Stage specs should store structured value/function/distribution specs, not frontend-only strings, so exact snapshots can lower into backend execution and manifests.\n- Sampling scope matters at the pipeline level: `per trial`, `per replicate`, `per run`, and `sweep` are different user intentions and need different provenance.\n\nThis should be an input to the next `0c46f69` implementation slice: the Evaluate-stage protocol editor can be built as a consumer of `bd5aefb` rather than hardcoding one-off controls for SISU and perturbations.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}